{"name":"Madder Red","hex":"#b7282e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"madder","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A herbaceous plant, Rubia tinctorum, native to Asia, cultivated for a red-purple dye (alizarin) obtained from the root.","The root of the plant, used as a medicine or a dye."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep reddish purple colour, like that of the dye."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/madder"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rubia tinctorum","blocks":[{"text":"Rubia tinctorum, the rose madder or common madder or dyer's madder, is a herbaceous perennial plant species belonging to the bedstraw and coffee family Rubiaceae. The type genus of the whole Rubiaceae family of around 80 flowering plants is called Rubia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Rubia_tinctorum_flowers.jpg/330px-Rubia_tinctorum_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubia_tinctorum","wikidata":"Q163641"},{"title":"Rubia","blocks":[{"text":"Rubia is the type genus of the Rubiaceae family of flowering plants, which also contains Coffea (coffee). It contains around 80 species of perennial scrambling or climbing herbs and subshrubs native to the Old World."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Rubia_tinctorum_002.JPG/330px-Rubia_tinctorum_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubia","wikidata":"Q162108"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Rubia_tinctorum_flowers.jpg/500px-Rubia_tinctorum_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Rubia_tinctorum_flowers.jpg/1280px-Rubia_tinctorum_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Rubia_tinctorum_flowers.jpg/500px-Rubia_tinctorum_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARubia_tinctorum_flowers.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Rubia_tinctorum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-123.jpg/330px-Rubia_tinctorum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-123.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Rubia_tinctorum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizina